  },
  "rules": {
    "oracle": "Reach, vigilance\nYou have no maximum hand size.\nEmbiggen Fist — Whenever you cast a spell that targets a creature you control, draw a card. Until end of turn, Ms. Marvel gains \"Ms. Marvel's base power is equal to the number of cards in your hand.\"",
    "cr": [
      "201.5",
      "603.2",
      "611.3a",
      "613.4b",
      "613.4c",
      "514.2",
      "402.2"
    ],
    "actual": "Casting a spell that targets a creature you control does nothing: no card is drawn and Ms. Marvel keeps her printed 1/4. The whole line is a single `Unimplemented granter_reference_unreached` ability; reach, vigilance and \"no maximum hand size\" work.",
    "expected": "Whenever you cast a spell that targets a creature you control, the trigger resolves before the spell (CR 603.3, 405.5): you draw a card, and until end of turn Ms. Marvel has an ability that sets her base power to the number of cards in your hand. It is a continuous effect from a static ability, so her power keeps tracking your hand size for the rest of the turn (CR 611.3a), in layer 7b (CR 613.4b), with pump effects and counters applied on top (CR 613.4c). At cleanup the granted ability ends (CR 514.2) and she is a 1/4 again.",
    "diagnosis": "The parser builds the trigger (SpellCast with a `Targets` creature-you-control filter, Draw, then a GenericEffect grant), but the granted static names its granter (\"Ms. Marvel's base power\"), so the parser masks the name as a granter reference. `granter_reference_unreached` (parser/oracle.rs:10033, applied by `demote_definitions` at parser/oracle.rs:9957, the guard added in #9423) then counts more granter references in the tree than the granter-symbol walk (`granter_symbols::node_fields`, types/ability_visit.rs:1199) reaches, and replaces the whole trigger with `Unimplemented granter_reference_unreached`. Here the granter and the object that gains the ability are the same permanent (\"Ms. Marvel gains ...\"), so there is no other object for the reference to bind to.",
    "suggested_fix": "When a \"<this object> gains \"<ability>\"\" grant targets the source itself, lower the source's name inside the granted text to the self reference (`SelfRef` / `Source`), as for any printed ability (CR 201.5: an object's name in its own ability text means that object), instead of a granter reference; the `granter_reference_unreached` guard then has nothing to refuse. The resulting shape is a `SpellCast` trigger (`valid_card: Typed { properties: [Targets(Typed Creature, controller You)] }`, `valid_target: Controller`, as Mockingbird, Ace Agent parses) executing `Draw 1` with a sequential sibling `GenericEffect { duration: UntilEndOfTurn, static_abilities: [Continuous { affected: SelfRef, modifications: [GrantStaticAbility(Continuous { affected: SelfRef, modifications: [SetPowerDynamic(HandSize { player: Controller })] })] }] }`. Regression test: cast a pump spell on Ms. Marvel with 7 other cards in hand and check the draw and the 8 + pump power, then that her power follows the hand size and resets at cleanup.",
    "override_note": "The patch replaces the unimplemented ability with that trigger, assembled from shapes the engine already runs: the SpellCast head of Mockingbird, Ace Agent, the self-targeted GenericEffect grant until end of turn of the manlands (Lavaclaw Reaches) and Chimeric Mass (which also grants a static ability), and `SetPowerDynamic` (layer 7b base power, like Aettir and Priwen) of `HandSize { Controller }` (like Body of Knowledge). The power must come from a granted static ability, not a one-shot `SetPowerDynamic` modification: a resolved one-shot effect would lock in the hand size at resolution, while \"base power is equal to the number of cards in your hand\" is a static ability whose value is checked continuously (CR 611.3a, 604.1). The tests show the draw, her power following the hand down and up during the turn, the +1/+1 counter and pump layered on top (CR 613.4c), the end at cleanup (CR 514.2), no cleanup discard (no maximum hand size, CR 402.2), and no trigger for a spell that targets only an opponent's creature. Reach and vigilance are untouched."
  },
